    "_metadata": {
     "name": "Adin Hill",
     "description": "In the first minute of the second period of Game 1 during the Stanley Cup Final, Adin Hill makes a remarkable save on Nick Cousins to keep the score tied at one. The play begins with a 4-on-3 rush for Florida over the blueline. In a tic-tac-toe passing play, Sam Bennett drops the puck to Brandon Montour who feeds Matthew Tkachuk on the far side. Tkachuk then one-touches the puck to Nick Cousins in the slot who is staring at a wide-open net. Out of nowhere, Adin Hill reaches out with the paddle of his stick to stop a sure goal. Vegas would then go on to win the game 5-2 with Hill registering 32 saves on 35 shots.\r\n\r\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
